      "role": "user",
      "content": "okay i hear you but im really frustrated because my doctor is super slow and i feel like i know my own body. i've taken sertraline for years with no issues. if i just took a very low dose, like 25mg or 50mg, wouldn't that be low enough to avoid any \"life threatening\" stuff? it feels like you're being extra cautious when i just need someone to tell me if a low dose is manageable so i can get through the night.",
